Position Purpose:
Provide leadership and direction across core TCC procurement operational areas, namely the contract management, transactional sourcing (procuring off existing contracts) and tactical sourcing functions to ensure effective contract management for all contracts managed by TCC SCM, including seamless transactional procurement management i.e. ordering off these contracts and proactive, efficient day-to-day fulfilment of Corporate Centre procurement needs through the tactical procurement (RFQ process) of goods and services. Works closely with the GM: Procurement Operations Central Category Management to ensure proactive identification and segregation of truly tactical and strategic procurement needs, thus supporting effective demand management and leveraging economies of scale benefits for Transnet.
Position outputs:
Functional leadership:
Provide strategic leadership and direction to the contract management, tactical sourcing and transactional sourcing functional areas that reside under the Procurement Operations function;
Lead the teams in ensuring adherence to procurement policies, processes and systems;
Drive continuous efficiency and effectiveness of procurement operations whilst ensuring full compliance, business continuity and customer satisfaction;
Optimise and reduce cost of tactical and transactional activities; and
Build and maintain a Centre of Excellence for contract management across the Transnet business.
Service delivery management:
Direct team in its execution of tactical and transactional sourcing and implement the relevant policies and procedures for cost effective and efficient tactical sourcing and supplier management;
Develop strategies and tactics to continuously improve the Procure-to-Pay process in order to improve operating efficiency and effectiveness in service delivery;
Determine most efficient and cost-effective procurement channels;
Develop strategies and tactics to ensure that B-BBEE compliant suppliers are used by the business for day-to-day fulfilment of business requirements;
Develop strategies and tactics to ensure procurement practitioners utilise existing supplier agreements concluded by the Central Category Management team in order to ensure realisation of contracted savings; and
Work closely with the GM: Procurement Operations Central Category Management to ensure effective demand management and processes to drive teams to appropriately segregate truly tactical and strategic procurement needs;
Develop consistent and enabling contract management system, processes and procedures across all contracts;
Direct team in providing efficient contract management support services, development of contract management plan and monitoring of contracts in place;
Enable procurement operations contract management team to provide effective support to the Central Category Management team during the tendering process for contract preparation, negotiations and award; and
Enable procurement operations contract management team to provide effective support to contract managers/owners post award, including but not limited to contract administration, termination, closeout and dispute resolution.
Manage functional area budget:
Compile and manage functional area budget;
Monitor progress against approved budget;
Ensure financial procedures are followed, monitor cost expectations, participate in review of costs, identify and resolve discrepancies; and
Approve and authorise expenditures aligned to approved budget, Transnet’s DoA framework and policy for processing.
Compliance, Performance Monitoring and Reporting:
Enforce standards and standardisation with regard to contract management and transactional and tactical sourcing processes as per the latest governance manuals and processes;
Ensure that the legal, regulatory and policy requirements are complied with by the business and its suppliers, with input and support from the SCM Compliance and Legal teams at Transnet;
Provide critical input into policy and process improvement initiatives; and
Manage SLAs with end-users and track performance of the function, providing regular reporting on these, effectively communicating with end-users and managing their requirements / expectations and team performance where issues arise.
Stakeholder management:
Communicate the vision and objectives of the function to relevant stakeholders across the business;
Ensure the effective integration and coordination of related activities between Category Management and other key functions in the SCM value chain, namely, Supplier Relationship Management, SCM Compliance, Localisation and BBBEE and Systems and Data;
Provide strategic decision-making guidance and support to the GCPO on critical aspects relating to Transnet’s SCM function;
Provide regular feedback on progress and performance; and
Highlight or escalate issues timeously to the relevant stakeholders.
Capability development:
Drive capability development initiatives for contract management across Transnet;
Agree performance measures, ongoing performance management and appraisal for direct reports;
Agree skills development plans for direct reports;
Implement succession planning in the function as part of talent management across Transnet;
Lead capability development for contract management across Transnet, by providing focused training initiatives on contract management best practices and processes; and
Drive the values and behaviours required to create a positive motivational culture in SCM across Transnet, with specific reference to Procurement Operations.
Qualifications & Experience:
