Description
Rand Refinery, established in 1920 is a single site integrated refinery, smelter, manufacturer of value added products of precious metals and technical assurance. We pride ourselves on our rich heritage which is rooted in integrity, honesty and excellence, backed by more than a century in gold refining. We are an LBMA good delivery accredited refinery and one of five LMBA referee in the world. Our products are accredited on various commodity exchanges and we have refined 99% (100 000 kg) of South Africa’s mined gold. We have refined over 130 000 kg – 150 000 kg of mined gold from rest of Africa. Our presence, accreditation and reputation allows South Africa to participate and monetise gold including:
Local presence of bullion banks & local bank liquidity;
Potential to work with gold producing countries;
Valuable cargo transporters;
Vaulting & storage
WHAT TO EXPECT
Working for Africa’s largest Refiner, Smelter and Fabricator of precious metals;
The best practical learning environment guided by a structured development plan;
On-the-job training as part of a committed customer focused team;
Regular feedback from Mentors;
Work Readiness training and development.
Requirements
REQUIREMENTS
National Diploma in Metallurgical or Chemical Engineering (in need of Inservice Training);
BTech./ BEng in Metallurgical or Chemical Engineering;
Must have an aggregate of 70% or higher in the above-mentioned fields of study.
DOCUMENTS TO SUBMIT WHEN APPLYING
2 page CV;
Certified copy of your ID document;
Certified copy of your matric certificate;
Certified copy of your academic record - this applies to those needing Inservice Training;
Certified copies of both your academic record and qualification (s) – this applies to those who have graduated with their BTech./BEng. qualifications.

